00:33:57.000 --> 00:35:06.000
They quickly phoned police, describing the perpetrator as between 35 and 45 years old, about 5'10 and 190 pounds, with a pointy stomach and a reddish-blonde crew card. He was wearing horn-rimmed eyeglasses and dressed unremarkably in trousers and a jacket. Officers Donald Fowke and Eric Zelms were on patrol east of Presidio when they received word of the attack and a description of the perpetrator. They raced towards the scene at Washington and Cherry, keeping their eyes peeled for a suspect as described. They soon spotted someone. A stocky, middle-aged white male with a light-colored crew card. Standing at about 5'10, the man walked slowly with his head bent down, not appearing to be in any hurry. Curiously, he matched the suspect's description to a tee, except that he was white.
他们迅速打电话给警察，将肇事者描述为35到45岁，身高约5英尺10英寸，体重190磅，有着尖尖的肚子和红金色的平头。他戴着角质框眼镜，穿着普通的裤子和夹克。唐纳德·福克警官和埃里克·泽尔姆斯警官在普雷西迪奥以东巡逻时，收到了袭击的消息和肇事者的描述。他们冲向华盛顿街和樱桃街的现场，睁大眼睛寻找描述中的嫌疑人。他们很快发现了一个人。一个身材敦实、中年白人男性，留着浅色平头。身高约5英尺10英寸，那人低着头慢慢走着，看起来并不着急。奇怪的是，他与嫌疑人的描述完全吻合，只是他是白人。

38
00:35:06.000 --> 00:36:04.000
The dispatcher had specifically said the offender was a black male. As the man didn't fit the profile, Officer Fowke and Zelms continued on. Upon arriving at the crime scene, officers found Paul Stein lying in a semi-supine position across the front seat with his head resting on the floor. Both he and the front compartment of the cab were soaked in blood. The three teenage siblings who had witnessed the aftermath of the shooting were interviewed at the scene. When they described the attacker as a white male, the questioning officer was confused. Weren't they on the lookout for a black suspect? Realizing the dispatcher had made a grave error, the officer immediately radioed in to have the broadcast corrected.
调度员明确表示罪犯是一名黑人男性。由于该男子不符合特征，福克警官和泽尔姆斯警官继续前行。到达犯罪现场后，警官们发现保罗·斯泰恩半仰着躺在前座上，头靠在地板上。他和出租车的前部都被鲜血浸透了。在现场采访了目睹枪击事件后果的三名青少年兄妹。当他们将袭击者描述为白人男性时，询问的警官感到困惑。他们不是在寻找一名黑人嫌疑人吗？意识到调度员犯了一个严重的错误，警官立即通过无线电要求更正广播。

39
00:36:04.000 --> 00:37:09.000
He then walked north along Cherry Street, eyes peeled for anyone who looked like the shooter. But the streets were quiet. Not only was there no one who matched the suspect's description, there weren't even any witnesses around to question. Continuing east along Jackson Street, the officer passed the man out walking his dog but didn't see anyone else noteworthy. When word reached officers Donald Fowke and Derek Zelms that the shooter was actually a white male, they were stunned. They had just passed by a man who matched the perpetrator's description in every way other than the colour of his skin. Realizing they might have inadvertently driven right by the killer, Officer Fowke sped off towards the Presidio War playground, believing the man probably headed there after turning onto Maple Street. The area was surrounded by dense foliage.
他随后沿着樱桃街向北走，仔细寻找任何看起来像枪手的人。但街道很安静。不仅没有人符合嫌疑人的描述，甚至连可以询问的目击者都没有。沿着杰克逊街继续向东走，警官经过一名遛狗的男子，但没有看到其他值得注意的人。当唐纳德·福克警官和德里克·泽尔姆斯警官得知枪手实际上是白人男性时，他们惊呆了。他们刚刚经过一名除了肤色外，在各方面都符合肇事者描述的男子。意识到他们可能无意中开车经过了凶手，福克警官加速驶向普雷西迪奥战争游乐场，认为那人在转入枫树街后可能去了那里。该地区被茂密的植被包围。

40
00:37:09.000 --> 00:38:06.000
Officer Fowke couldn't say anything through the dark. A large-scale search commenced. A spotlight scanned the darkened streets, alleyways and parklands as police swarmed the area in patrol cars and on motorbikes. Some paced the streets with sniffer dogs in tow. But the killer was long gone. Paul Stein's logbook indicated that the killer's destination had been the corner of Washington and Maple Street. The intersection was guarded by high trees that obstructed the views from residential windows, making it a safe place to pull off the murder without witnesses. It was also only one block from the Presidio War playground which would have provided a quick escape route.
福克警官在黑暗中什么也看不见。大规模搜捕开始了。探照灯扫过黑暗的街道、小巷和公园，警察们乘坐巡逻车和摩托车蜂拥而至。一些人带着嗅探犬在街上踱步。但凶手早已逃之夭夭。保罗·斯泰恩的日志显示，凶手的目的地是华盛顿街和枫树街的拐角处。交叉路口被高大的树木遮挡，阻挡了住宅窗户的视线，使其成为一个可以在没有目击者的情况下实施谋杀的安全地点。它距离普雷西迪奥战争游乐场也只有一个街区，这本可以提供一条快速逃生路线。

41
00:38:06.000 --> 00:39:26.000
However, the location where Paul's cab was found was one block further west in a more exposed spot further from the park. Police wondered if Paul had perhaps overshot the intersection and the killer asked him to pull over at the next corner. Or maybe the shooter saw an unexpected witness at the original destination and changed his mind at the last moment. Another possibility was that Paul had still been driving when he was shot, forcing the gunman to take control of the vehicle as it careened out of control. There was very little evidence to help identify the suspect, yet police had a couple of clues to go on. Despite the killer's attempts to wipe the cab clean of evidence, several latent bloody fingerprints were lifted from the exterior of the vehicle. A pair of men's size 7 black leather gloves were also found inside the cab. These didn't belong to Paul. Examination of a spent Winchester Western bullet casing found on the passenger seat confirmed that it had been shot from a 9mm semi-automatic pistol.
然而，发现保罗出租车的地方在更西边一个街区，位置更暴露，距离公园更远。警方怀疑保罗是否可能开过了交叉路口，凶手让他停在下一个拐角处。或者枪手在最初的目的地看到了意想不到的目击者，并在最后一刻改变了主意。另一种可能性是，保罗在被枪击时仍在驾驶，迫使枪手在车辆失控时接管了控制权。几乎没有什么证据可以帮助识别嫌疑人，但警方有一些线索。尽管凶手试图擦掉出租车上的证据，但从车辆外部提取了几枚潜在的血指纹。车内还发现了一副男式7码黑色皮手套。这些不属于保罗。对在乘客座位上发现的一枚已发射的温彻斯特西部子弹壳的检查证实，它是从一把9毫米半自动手枪中射出的。

42
00:39:26.000 --> 00:40:30.000
The killer had also taken Paul's wallet and car keys before fleeing the scene. This indicated to police that the shooting was nothing more than a violent robbery and there was no reason to believe otherwise. The three teenagers who'd seen the killer worked with a police artist to create a suspect sketch. Officer Fowke later helped complete a second composite based on the man he'd passed near the crime scene. The two faces were remarkably similar. Soon, both were on display in police stations across the state, printed side by side on wanted posters. Two days after Paul's murder, Carol Fisher-Cottes was sitting at her desk at the San Francisco Chronicle newspaper. She worked as the letters editor and it was her job to sort through correspondence sent by readers.
凶手在逃离现场前还拿走了保罗的钱包和车钥匙。这向警方表明，枪击事件不过是一起暴力抢劫，没有理由相信其他情况。看到凶手的三名青少年与警方画像师合作绘制了一张嫌疑人素描。福克警官后来协助完成了第二张基于他在犯罪现场附近经过的那名男子的合成图。两张脸非常相似。很快，两者都在全州的警察局展出，并排印在通缉令海报上。保罗遇害两天后，卡罗尔·费舍尔-科特斯正坐在旧金山纪事报的办公桌前。她担任信件编辑，她的工作是整理读者寄来的信件。

43
00:40:30.000 --> 00:41:21.000
As she flicked through the mail that had arrived that day, she spotted an unusual envelope. In the top left hand corner where a return address was usually printed, someone had drawn a small crosshair symbol. Carol opened the envelope and, to her alarm, a strip of bloodied cloth fell out onto the desk. She looked inside the envelope and saw a single sheet of paper. It was a brief handwritten letter that read, This is the Zodiac speaking. I am the murderer of the taxi driver over by Washington and Maple Street last night. To prove this, here is a bloodstained piece of his shirt.
当她翻阅当天收到的邮件时，她发现了一个不寻常的信封。在通常印有回信地址的左上角，有人画了一个小小的十字准星符号。卡罗尔打开信封，令她惊恐的是，一条带血的布片掉到了桌子上。她往信封里看去，看到了一张纸。这是一封简短的手写信，上面写着：“我是黄道十二宫。我就是昨晚在华盛顿街和枫树街附近谋杀出租车司机的凶手。为了证明这一点，这是他衬衫上的一块血迹斑斑的碎片。”

44
00:41:21.000 --> 00:42:17.000
I am the same man who did in the people in the North Bay area. The San Francisco police could have caught me last night if they had searched the park properly instead of holding road races with their motorcycles seeing who could make the most noise. The car drivers should have just parked their cars and sat there quietly, waiting for me to come out of cover. School children make nice targets. I think I shall wipe out a school bus some morning. Just shoot out the front tyre and then pick off the kitties as they come bouncing out. The letter was signed off with the same crosshair symbol that appeared on the envelope. Law enforcement officials were notified about the Zodiac's latest confession and took possession of the letter.
我就是那个在北湾地区杀人的凶手。如果旧金山警方昨晚能好好搜查公园，而不是开着摩托车在那儿比谁的噪音大，他们本可以抓住我的。那些开车的人应该直接把车停好，静静地坐在车里，等着我从掩体里出来。小学生是很好的目标。我想哪天早上我要毁掉一辆校车。只要打爆前轮胎，然后等那些小家伙蹦出来时把他们一个个干掉。这封信的落款处画着和信封上一样的十字准星符号。执法部门收到了“黄道十二宫”最新的供词，并扣押了这封信。

45
00:42:17.000 --> 00:43:05.000
Given that Paul Stein's murder had been classed as a violent robbery, detectives hadn't considered any links to the Zodiac killer. So far, he'd only confessed to murders involving young couples in isolated locales. Because the Zodiac had been particularly brutal towards his female victims, criminal analysts theorized that he had a particular hatred for young women. A male cab driver killed at work didn't fit with his ammo. Additionally, detectives weren't even aware that a piece of Paul Stein's shirt was missing. No one had noticed this detail when bagging his clothing as evidence.
由于保罗·斯坦的谋杀案被归类为暴力抢劫，侦探们并没有考虑其与“黄道十二宫”杀手之间的任何联系。到目前为止，他只承认了涉及偏僻地区年轻情侣的谋杀案。由于“黄道十二宫”对女性受害者特别残忍，犯罪分析师推测他对年轻女性有特殊的仇恨。一名在工作中被杀的男性出租车司机并不符合他的作案手法。此外，侦探们甚至不知道保罗·斯坦的衬衫少了一块。在将他的衣服作为证据装袋时，没有人注意到这个细节。

46
00:43:05.000 --> 00:44:00.000
They recovered Paul's shirt from the morgue and compared it to the strip of blooded cloth sent to the Chronicle. It was a perfect match. However, it appeared the killer had taken more fabric that was still unaccounted for. A handwriting expert for the FBI compared this letter with the others sent by the Zodiac killer and deemed that all had likely been written by the same person. With another Zodiac murder confirmed, criminal analysts now had more information to work with. They noticed how the killer's letters were peppered with misspelled words and grammatical errors. He seemed intelligent, so these mistakes suggested he lacked a formal education.
他们从停尸房找回了保罗的衬衫，并将其与寄给《纪事报》的那块带血的布条进行了比对。完全吻合。然而，凶手似乎还拿走了更多尚未找到的布料。联邦调查局的一名笔迹专家将这封信与“黄道十二宫”杀手寄出的其他信件进行了比对，认为所有信件很可能出自同一人之手。随着又一起“黄道十二宫”谋杀案得到证实，犯罪分析师现在有了更多可供研究的信息。他们注意到凶手的信件中充斥着拼写错误和语法错误。他看起来很聪明，所以这些错误表明他缺乏正规教育。

47
00:44:00.000 --> 00:45:02.000
Though, it was also possible he was deliberately making mistakes, just to throw authorities off track. Another common thread was the fact that all of his crimes seemed to occur by bodies of water or in places with water-themed names. None of his crimes appeared personally motivated. It seemed that all victims had simply been in the wrong place at the wrong time. This was extremely concerning, given that the window between his attacks was narrowing. After shooting David Faraday and Betty Lou Jensen, almost seven months passed before the Zodiac killer struck again. Then, there were only three months between his attacks against Michael Majo and Darlene Farron and Brian Hartnell and Cecilia Shepard. Paul Stein's attack came exactly two weeks later.
不过，也有可能他是故意犯错，只是为了误导当局。另一个共同点是，他所有的犯罪似乎都发生在水体附近或地名与水有关的地方。他的犯罪似乎都没有个人动机。所有的受害者似乎都只是在错误的时间出现在了错误的地点。考虑到他作案的间隔时间正在缩短，这非常令人担忧。在枪杀大卫·法拉第和贝蒂·卢·詹森后，过了近七个月“黄道十二宫”杀手才再次作案。然后，他袭击迈克尔·马乔和达琳·法伦，以及布莱恩·哈特内尔和塞西莉亚·谢泼德之间仅隔了三个月。保罗·斯坦遇袭则是在两周后。

48
00:45:02.000 --> 00:46:11.000
If he continued following this pattern, it seemed likely that another murder was imminent. When newspapers reported on the Zodiac's latest letter, they strategically declined to mention the threat he'd made about killing schoolchildren. California's residents were panicked enough, and they didn't want the Zodiac to get any more satisfaction. That all changed on October 16, five days after Paul Stein's murder, when the Los Angeles Times decided to make the detail public. As expected, the result was widespread panic. On the afternoon of October 20, a couple was out walking with their eight-year-old daughter in the northern California town of Ucaya. As the trio strolled along the quiet back road of Lake Mendocino Drive, a light-colored car drove by. The driver threw a twig out the window towards them.
如果他继续遵循这种模式，很可能很快就会发生另一起谋杀案。当报纸报道“黄道十二宫”的最新信件时，他们策略性地没有提及他关于杀害小学生的威胁。加州居民已经够恐慌了，他们不想让“黄道十二宫”得到更多的满足感。这一切在10月16日，即保罗·斯坦遇害五天后发生了变化，当时《洛杉矶时报》决定将这一细节公之于众。不出所料，结果引发了广泛的恐慌。10月20日下午，一对夫妇带着他们八岁的女儿在加州北部的尤卡亚镇散步。当三人沿着门多西诺湖大道那条安静的后路漫步时，一辆浅色的汽车开了过去。司机从窗户向他们扔了一根树枝。

49
00:46:11.000 --> 00:46:56.000
Attached was a piece of paper. Written on it in crude handwriting were the words, Your Next, Zee. The following day, a San Francisco Bay Area newspaper received a phone call from someone claiming to be the Zodiac. He issued a harrowing warning. He was planning to shoot children as they traveled on school buses. Both incidents were reported, and law enforcement agencies were immediately on high alert. The police and California's highway patrol began surveilling all school buses in the area.
上面系着一张纸。上面用粗糙的笔迹写着：“下一个就是你，Zee”。第二天，旧金山湾区的一家报纸接到一个自称是“黄道十二宫”的人打来的电话。他发出了令人毛骨悚然的警告。他计划在孩子们乘坐校车时开枪射杀他们。这两起事件都被报道了，执法机构立即进入高度戒备状态。警方和加州公路巡警开始监视该地区所有的校车。

50
00:46:56.000 --> 00:48:02.000
Some even had officers on board, ready to respond if necessary. But there were no attacks. It was becoming abundantly clear that the media obsession had spurred hoaxes and attention seekers into action, prompting false confessions and copycats. Some individuals developed an unhealthy fixation with the case, including one man from Montana who was convinced he was going to be a victim. I left California because it got too hot for me, an individual claiming to be the Zodiac told an Oklahoma radio program. The Zodiac was a title many were willing to adopt for their own reasons, while the actual killer remained silent. To coax the Zodiac killer out of hiding, California's Attorney General appealed for him to come forward by promising to provide help and protection.
有些车上甚至有警官随行，准备在必要时做出反应。但并没有发生袭击。显而易见，媒体的痴迷已经促使恶作剧者和寻求关注的人采取行动，导致了虚假的供词和模仿犯罪。一些人对这个案件产生了不健康的执念，包括一名来自蒙大拿州的男子，他坚信自己会成为受害者。“我离开了加州，因为那里对我来说太危险了，”一名自称是“黄道十二宫”的人告诉俄克拉荷马州的一个广播节目。许多人出于各自的原因愿意采用“黄道十二宫”这个称号，而真正的凶手却保持沉默。为了诱使“黄道十二宫”杀手现身，加州总检察长呼吁他自首，并承诺提供帮助和保护。

51
00:48:02.000 --> 00:48:55.000
Editors at the San Francisco Examiner also ran a direct message to the Zodiac on the paper's front page. It read, in part, Five people are dead. Let there be no more killings. You are being hunted everywhere in the state and nation. You are alone in this world. You can share your secrets with no one. We ask that you give yourself up to the examiner. We offer you no protection and no sympathy, but we do offer you fair treatment, the assurance of medical help, and the full benefits of your legal rights. And we offer to tell your story. There was no response.
《旧金山考察家报》的编辑们也在报纸头版刊登了给“黄道十二宫”的直接信息。内容部分写道：“五个人已经死了。不要再有杀戮了。你在全州和全国范围内都被追捕。在这个世界上你是孤独的。你不能与任何人分享你的秘密。我们要求你向《考察家报》自首。我们不提供保护，也不提供同情，但我们提供公平的对待、医疗救助的保证以及你法律权利的全部利益。我们还提议讲述你的故事。”没有回应。

52
00:48:55.000 --> 00:50:01.000
Paul Stein's brother Joe also directly addressed the Zodiac when he offered himself up as bait. Joe was sure that he could take the killer down, explaining that he was an Army and Air Force veteran capable of overpowering a coward like the Zodiac, even without a weapon. Giving specific details as to where the killer could find him, Joe said, I work at the Richfield service station at 706 Sutter Street in Modesto. I start at 7am. I go to lunch at the walk-in chicken in a shopping centre two blocks away, riding a bicycle along Sutter Street and leaving the station at noon each day. I go back to the service station and work until five. Let him come and get me. Other residents and business owners in the neighbourhood were less than thrilled about Joe's challenge.
保罗·斯坦的兄弟乔也直接向“黄道十二宫”喊话，提出自己作为诱饵。乔确信他能制服凶手，并解释说他是一名陆军和空军退伍军人，即使没有武器也能制服像“黄道十二宫”这样的懦夫。乔给出了凶手可以找到他的具体细节，他说：“我在莫德斯托萨特街706号的里奇菲尔德加油站工作。我早上7点上班。我每天中午离开加油站，骑自行车沿着萨特街去两个街区外的快餐店吃午饭。我回到加油站工作到五点。让他来抓我吧。”社区里的其他居民和店主对乔的挑战并不感到兴奋。

53
00:50:01.000 --> 00:51:09.000
They feared it would draw the serial killer to their community and place them in danger. However, their concern was unwarranted. The Zodiac didn't take Joe up on his offer. On the night of Saturday, October 18, a lone car sat in the parking lot of Vallejo's Blue Rock Springs Park, close by to where Darlene Farron and Michael Majo had been shot. It was nearing 2am when a second vehicle approached. A 1964 Greenish Grey Chevrolet station wagon pulled into the parking lot and drove towards the other car. The Chevrolet stopped and its engine switched off. A middle-aged man of average height and build exited the vehicle. He walked right up to the neighbouring car. Just then, two undercover officers sprang into action.
他们担心这会把连环杀手引到他们的社区，使他们处于危险之中。然而，他们的担忧是多余的。“黄道十二宫”并没有接受乔的提议。10月18日星期六晚上，一辆孤零零的汽车停在瓦列霍蓝石泉公园的停车场里，靠近达琳·法伦和迈克尔·马乔被枪杀的地方。快到凌晨2点时，第二辆车靠近了。一辆1964年的灰绿色雪佛兰旅行车驶入停车场，朝另一辆车开去。雪佛兰停了下来，引擎熄火了。一名中等身材、中等体型的中年男子下了车。他径直走向旁边的车。就在这时，两名卧底警官采取了行动。

54
00:51:09.000 --> 00:52:00.000
They had planted the first car there as bait, hoping to lure the Zodiac into attempting another attack. Their plan appeared to have worked. But the driver of the Chevrolet explained that he was a Navy employee stationed on Treasure Island in San Francisco. He was on his way to Lake Berryessa, but had gotten lost. Upon seeing the car at Blue Rock Springs Park, he decided to ask for directions. With no reason to doubt him, the officers let the man go and resumed their covert positions. They stayed there for the rest of the night, but nobody else approached the bait car. The Zodiac clearly wasn't falling for it.
他们把第一辆车停在那里作为诱饵，希望能引诱“黄道十二宫”再次发动袭击。他们的计划似乎奏效了。但雪佛兰的司机解释说，他是驻扎在旧金山金银岛的一名海军雇员。他正要去伯耶萨湖，但迷路了。看到蓝石泉公园里的车，他决定问路。由于没有理由怀疑他，警官们放走了那个人，并恢复了他们的隐蔽位置。他们在那里待了剩下的时间，但没有其他人靠近诱饵车。显然，“黄道十二宫”并没有上当。

55
00:52:00.000 --> 00:53:05.000
Despite their initial hope, the tactic was unsuccessful and no further stakeouts were planned. Investigators turned their focus to the guns used during the attacks. In total, the killer had used three different firearms. A .22 caliber weapon had been used on David and Betty Lou, while two different 9mm weapons were used during the attacks on Michael and Darlene and Paul Stein. The one used to kill Paul was a semi-automatic that required ammunition only available from specialised gun dealers. Only 143 9mm firearms similar to those used in the Zodiac attacks had been sold in San Francisco over the last three years. Investigators hunted down the buyer's gun applications and compared their handwriting to that on the Zodiac letters.
尽管最初抱有希望，但该策略并不成功，也没有计划进一步的蹲守。调查人员将重点转向了袭击中使用的枪支。凶手总共使用了三种不同的枪支。大卫和贝蒂·卢遇害时使用的是.22口径武器，而在袭击迈克尔、达琳和保罗·斯坦时使用了两种不同的9毫米武器。杀死保罗的那把是半自动手枪，需要专门的枪支经销商才能买到的弹药。过去三年里，旧金山仅售出了143把与“黄道十二宫”袭击中使用的类似的9毫米枪支。调查人员追查了购枪申请，并将他们的笔迹与“黄道十二宫”信件上的笔迹进行了比对。

56
00:53:05.000 --> 00:54:03.000
No matches were found. It was close to midnight on Tuesday, October 21, 1969, when a phone rang at Oakland Police Department, 12.5 miles east of San Francisco. An officer answered and was greeted by a male on the other line who introduced himself as the Zodiac killer. He then made a strange request. He wanted one of two specific defense attorneys to appear on San Francisco talk show, the Jim Dunbar show, the following morning. If this request was granted, the caller said he would be open to negotiating live on air. To prove he was genuine, he provided knowledge about the Zodiac case that police deemed to be legitimate.
没有发现匹配项。1969年10月21日星期二午夜时分，旧金山以东12.5英里的奥克兰警察局电话响了。一名警官接听电话，电话那头的一名男子自称是“黄道十二宫”杀手。他提出了一个奇怪的要求。他希望两位特定辩护律师中的一位能在第二天早上出现在旧金山的脱口秀节目《吉姆·邓巴秀》上。如果这个要求得到满足，打电话的人说他愿意在直播中进行谈判。为了证明他是真的，他提供了警方认为合法的关于“黄道十二宫”案件的知识。

57
00:54:03.000 --> 00:54:51.000
Investigators agreed to the caller's demands. One of the attorneys he wanted to speak to was Melvin Belier. He was famous for defending Jack Ruby, an American nightclub owner who killed presidential assassin Lee Harvey Oswald. Belier agreed to appear on the show. The next morning, the Jim Dunbar show went live to air at seven o'clock. All the other guests on the show were canceled as Dunbar and Belier made small talk. After 49 minutes, the phone finally rang. The caller identified himself as the Zodiac, but Belier asked for another name they could use.
调查人员同意了打电话者的要求。他想与之交谈的律师之一是梅尔文·贝利。他因辩护杰克·鲁比而闻名，杰克·鲁比是一名杀害总统刺客李·哈维·奥斯瓦尔德的美国夜总会老板。贝利同意参加节目。第二天早上，吉姆·邓巴秀在七点钟直播。节目中的所有其他嘉宾都被取消了，邓巴和贝利进行了闲聊。49分钟后，电话终于响了。打电话的人自称是“黄道十二宫”，但贝利要求换一个他们可以使用的名字。

58
00:54:51.000 --> 00:55:18.000
He told them to call him Sam. Talk to us. Just tell us what's going on inside you right now, Sam. I have headaches. How long have you had those headaches, Sam? In a long time? Since I killed a kid. If it all boils down to the question of you're giving yourself up if you could be assured that you wouldn't get capital punishment for myself.
他告诉他们叫他萨姆。“跟我们谈谈。告诉我们你现在内心在想什么，萨姆。”“我头疼。”“萨姆，你头疼多久了？很久了吗？”“自从我杀了一个孩子。如果这一切归结为你是否会自首的问题，如果你能被保证不会被判死刑的话……”

59
00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:51.000
I don't want to give myself up. So when I kill those kids... In an effort to avoid having the call traced, Sam kept hanging up and calling back minutes later. In total, he phoned 15 times over the course of two hours. Before ending one call, Sam said, I'm getting one of my headaches now. I've got to kill. I've got to kill.
“我不想自首。所以当我杀那些孩子的时候……”为了避免电话被追踪，萨姆不断挂断电话，几分钟后再打过来。在两个小时内，他总共打了15次电话。在结束其中一个电话前，萨姆说：“我现在又开始头疼了。我必须杀人。我必须杀人。”

60
00:55:51.000 --> 00:56:47.000
At one point, he threatened to jump off the roof of a hotel unless Belier agreed to meet him there. While off air, Belier convinced Sam to meet him elsewhere. They arranged to meet at 10.30 that morning at the St. Vincent de Paul's office building on Mission Street. Belier and Dunbar went to the location with high hopes. Word about the meeting got out and camera crews and curious onlookers flocked to the area hoping to witness some action. The police arrived half an hour later, but the Zodiac never showed up. Recordings of the calls were played to three people who had heard the Zodiac's voice. These were Lake Berryessa survivor Brian Hartnell and the two police dispatchers Nancy Slover and David Slade.
有一次，他威胁说要从一家酒店的屋顶跳下去，除非贝利同意在那里见他。在节目外，贝利说服萨姆在别处见面。他们约定当天上午10点30分在米申街的圣文森特·德·保罗办公大楼见面。贝利和邓巴怀着极大的希望前往该地点。关于这次会面的消息传开了，摄像组和好奇的围观者涌向该地区，希望能目睹一些动静。警察半小时后赶到，但“黄道十二宫”从未露面。电话录音被播放给三位听过“黄道十二宫”声音的人听。他们是伯耶萨湖幸存者布莱恩·哈特内尔和两名警察调度员南希·斯洛弗和戴维·斯莱德。

61
00:56:47.000 --> 00:57:43.000
None of them thought Sam sounded like the Zodiac. With no evidence to convince them otherwise, police suspected that the calls had been a hoax. On Saturday, November 8, another envelope arrived at the San Francisco Chronicle with the words, please rush to the editor, written on both sides. It had been almost four weeks since the Zodiac had made contact. He was now attempting to be funny by submitting a greeting card that parodied a popular television commercial of the time. On the front was an illustration of a fountain pen dripping in blood and inside was a cipher with 340 different characters. Accompanying the card was a handwritten letter that read,
他们都不认为萨姆听起来像“黄道十二宫”。由于没有证据让他们相信这一点，警方怀疑这些电话是恶作剧。11月8日星期六，另一个信封寄到了《旧金山纪事报》，两面都写着“请速交编辑”。距离“黄道十二宫”上次联系已经过去了近四周。他现在试图通过提交一张模仿当时流行电视广告的贺卡来搞笑。正面是一幅滴着血的钢笔插图，里面是一个包含340个不同字符的密码。随卡附上的一封手写信写道：

62
00:57:43.000 --> 00:58:20.000
This is the Zodiac speaking. I thought you would need a good laugh before you hear the bad news. You won't get the news for a while yet. P.S. could you print this new cipher on your front page? I get awfully lonely when I am ignored. So lonely, I could do my thing. It was signed with the Zodiac's crosshair symbol followed by the words, December, July, August, September, October equals 7.
“我是‘黄道十二宫’。我想在听到坏消息之前，你需要好好笑一笑。你暂时还不会得到消息。附：你能把这个新密码印在头版吗？被忽视时我感到非常孤独。太孤独了，我可能会做我的事。”落款是“黄道十二宫”的十字准星符号，后面跟着“12月、7月、8月、9月、10月等于7”的字样。

63
00:58:20.000 --> 00:59:00.000
This final line was explained the very next day when the San Francisco Chronicle received another letter that began. This is the Zodiac speaking. Up to the end of October I have killed seven people. I have grown rather angry with the police for their telling lies about me. So I shall change the way the collecting of slaves. I shall no longer announce to anyone. When I commit my murders they shall look like routine robberies, killings of anger and a few fake accidents, etc.
最后一行在第二天得到了解释，当时《旧金山纪事报》收到了另一封信，开头写道：“我是‘黄道十二宫’。到10月底，我已经杀了七个人。我对警察关于我的谎言感到非常愤怒。所以我将改变收集奴隶的方式。我将不再向任何人宣布。当我犯下谋杀案时，它们看起来就像例行的抢劫、愤怒的杀戮和一些伪造的事故等。”

64
00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:47.000
The police shall never catch me because I have been too clever for them. The Zodiac's claim that he'd killed seven people was confusing as he was only known to have taken the lives of five victims. He went on to boast that he avoided detection by wearing a disguise and coating his fingertips with airplane cement while committing his crimes. He also claimed to have wiped Paul Stein's cab down to leave the police with false clues. Then detailed a supposed encounter he'd had with two officers near the scene. Quote, Two cops pulled a goof about three minutes after I left the cab.
“警察永远抓不到我，因为我比他们聪明得多。”“黄道十二宫”声称他杀了七个人，这令人困惑，因为已知他只夺走了五名受害者的生命。他接着吹嘘说，他在犯罪时通过伪装和用飞机胶水涂抹指尖来避免被发现。他还声称擦拭了保罗·斯坦的出租车，给警方留下了错误的线索。然后详细描述了他曾在现场附近与两名警官的所谓相遇。引用：“我离开出租车大约三分钟后，两个警察搞砸了。

65
00:59:47.000 --> 01:00:29.000
I was walking down the hill to the park when this cop car pulled up and one of them called me over and asked if I saw anyone acting suspicious or strange in the last five to ten minutes. And I said yes. There was this man who was running by waving a gun and the cops peeled rubber and went around the corner as I directed them. And I disappeared into the park a block and a half away, never to be seen again. Hey pig, doesn't it roll you up to have your nose rubbed in your boo-boos? The letter droned on for six pages.
我正走下山去公园，这时警车停了下来，其中一个叫住我，问我过去五到十分钟内是否看到有人行为可疑或奇怪。我说有。有一个人跑过去挥舞着枪，警察猛踩油门，按照我的指示绕过拐角。而我消失在了一个半街区外的公园里，再也没有被看见。嘿，猪猡，把你的鼻子按在你的错误里，这难道不让你感到羞耻吗？”这封信喋喋不休地写了六页。

66
01:00:29.000 --> 01:01:15.000
Towards the end, the Zodiac provided accurate bomb-making instructions along with an illustration of a homemade incendiary device. He warned he was going to use this contraption to blow up a bus, adding that he could be storing it in his basement or at the site where he intended to detonate. On his trademark crosshair symbol, the Zodiac had added small X's at various points of the circle, which were believed to indicate various times of day. Editors for the San Francisco Chronicle published excerpts from the two most recent letters, but decided to omit the bomb threat for fear it would lead to panic.
在结尾处，“黄道十二宫”提供了准确的炸弹制造说明，并附上了自制燃烧装置的插图。他警告说他要用这个装置炸毁一辆公共汽车，并补充说他可能把它存放在地下室或他打算引爆的地点。在标志性的十字准星符号上，“黄道十二宫”在圆圈的各个点上添加了小X，据信这代表了一天中的不同时间。《旧金山纪事报》的编辑们发表了最近两封信的摘录，但决定删掉炸弹威胁，以免引起恐慌。

67
01:01:15.000 --> 01:02:07.000
They also published the new cipher included with the greeting card, which was named the 340 cipher. It was a different code altogether from the original 408 cipher, and the editors hoped that amateur code breakers would be able to crack this one too. It was also forwarded to professional cryptologists at the FBI headquarters, the National Security Agency, and the Central Intelligence Agency. But no one was able to break the code. In December 1969, defence lawyer Melvin Beley travelled to the German city of Munich to attend a conference. While he was away, his housekeeper back in San Francisco forwarded all correspondence to his office
他们还发表了贺卡中包含的新密码，即“340密码”。这与最初的“408密码”完全不同，编辑们希望业余密码破译者也能破解这个密码。它也被转发给了联邦调查局总部、国家安全局和中央情报局的专业密码学家。但没有人能破解这个密码。1969年12月，辩护律师梅尔文·贝利前往德国慕尼黑参加会议。在他离开期间，他在旧金山的管家将所有信件转发到了他的办公室，

68
01:02:07.000 --> 01:02:52.000
so his employees could check for important documents. When they returned to work after the Christmas break, they discovered an envelope postmarked December 20. Scribbled on the back in poor spelling was the message, Merry Christmas and New Year. One of Beley's colleagues opened the envelope. Inside was a blood-stained scrap of fabric along with a neatly handwritten letter that read, Dear Melvin, this is the Zodiac speaking. I wish you a happy Christmas. The one thing I ask of you is this, please help me.
以便他的员工可以检查重要文件。圣诞假期后他们回到工作岗位时，发现了一个邮戳为12月20日的信封。背面用糟糕的拼写潦草地写着：“圣诞快乐，新年快乐”。贝利的一位同事打开了信封。里面是一块带血的布料，还有一封整洁的手写信，上面写着：“亲爱的梅尔文，我是‘黄道十二宫’。祝你圣诞快乐。我请求你的一件事是，请帮帮我。

69
01:02:52.000 --> 01:03:41.000
I cannot reach out for help because this thing in me won't let me. I am binding it extremely difficult to hold it in check. I am afraid I will lose control again and take my ninth and possibly tenth victim. Please help me, I am drowning. At the moment the children are safe from the bomb because it is so massive to dig in and the trigger mechanism required much work to get it adjusted just right. But if I hold back too long from number nine, I will lose all control of myself and set the bomb up. Please help me, I cannot remain in control for much longer.
我无法寻求帮助，因为我体内的这个东西不让我这样做。我发现很难控制它。我担心我会再次失去控制，夺走我的第九个甚至第十个受害者。请帮帮我，我快淹死了。目前孩子们是安全的，因为炸弹太大了，难以挖掘，触发机制需要大量工作才能调整得恰到好处。但如果我推迟第九个受害者太久，我就会完全失去控制，安装炸弹。请帮帮我，我无法再保持控制太久了。”

70
01:03:41.000 --> 01:04:24.000
The envelope and its contents were passed along to authorities, who determined that the bloody fabric was another piece of Paul Stein's shirt. This, along with the fact that the Zodiac's bomb threat hadn't been released to the public, convinced them that the letter was genuine. Although it was significantly neater than the others, leading some to believe that the Zodiac wanted to impress Belai. It was difficult to tell whether the Zodiac was being sincere or sarcastic in his cries for help. Up until this point, he'd portrayed himself as a dangerous man not to be messed with,
信封及其内容被移交给当局，他们确定带血的布料是保罗·斯坦衬衫的另一部分。这一点，加上“黄道十二宫”的炸弹威胁没有向公众发布的事实，使他们确信这封信是真的。尽管它比其他的要整洁得多，导致一些人认为“黄道十二宫”想给贝利留下深刻印象。很难说“黄道十二宫”在求救时是真诚的还是讽刺的。直到这一点，他一直把自己描绘成一个不可招惹的危险人物，

71
01:04:24.000 --> 01:05:07.000
but now he was coming across as vulnerable and desperate. It was also unclear what he wanted Belai to do with this information, as he hadn't specifically requested psychiatric or legal help. But the letter raised an even bigger question. At this point, the Zodiac had been linked to five murders, those of Betty Lou Jensen, David Faraday, Darlene Farron, Cecilia Shepard and Paul Stein. So who were the three other victims he was referring to? Were there more victims investigators hadn't yet linked him to?
但现在他表现得脆弱而绝望。也不清楚他希望贝利如何处理这些信息，因为他没有明确要求精神病学或法律援助。但这封信提出了一个更大的问题。此时，“黄道十二宫”已与五起谋杀案有关，即贝蒂·卢·詹森、大卫·法拉第、达琳·法伦、塞西莉亚·谢泼德和保罗·斯坦。那么他提到的另外三名受害者是谁？是否还有调查人员尚未将他联系起来的更多受害者？

72
01:05:07.000 --> 01:05:58.000
Or was he simply taunting them? Belai appealed for the Zodiac to make further contact via an article in the San Francisco Chronicle. He offered to meet anywhere the Zodiac wanted and agree to any demands. On January 14, 1970, the phone rang at Belai's home in San Francisco. He was still overseas, so his housekeeper took the call. It was Sam, the same man who had called the Jim Dunbar show claiming to be the Zodiac. When he was told the lawyer wasn't available, Sam replied, I can't wait, it's my birthday.
还是他只是在嘲弄他们？贝利通过《旧金山纪事报》的一篇文章呼吁“黄道十二宫”进一步联系。他提议在“黄道十二宫”想要的任何地方见面，并同意任何要求。1970年1月14日，贝利在旧金山的家中电话响了。他还在海外，所以他的管家接了电话。是萨姆，那个曾打电话给《吉姆·邓巴秀》自称是“黄道十二宫”的人。当被告知律师不在时，萨姆回答说：“我等不及了，今天是我的生日。”

73
01:05:58.000 --> 01:06:51.000
He then hung up the phone. Almost a month later on February 5, Sam called Jim Dunbar again. Police were alerted and Jim tried to keep Sam talking while detectives raced to the studios to listen in. By the time they arrived, Sam had hung up. The call hadn't been long enough to be traced. The calls from Sam also continued at Melvin Belai's residence, so the FBI set up a trace on the line. One call was eventually traced back to a mental health facility in Oakland. It had been made by an inpatient named Eric Wheel, who was an amateur photographer from the San Francisco Bay Area.
然后他挂断了电话。近一个月后的2月5日，萨姆再次致电吉姆·邓巴。警方接到警报，吉姆试图让萨姆保持通话，而侦探们则赶往演播室监听。当他们到达时，萨姆已经挂断了。通话时间不够长，无法追踪。萨姆的电话也继续打到梅尔文·贝利的住所，所以联邦调查局在电话线上设置了追踪。一个电话最终被追踪到奥克兰的一家心理健康机构。这是由一名叫埃里克·威尔的住院病人打出的，他是旧金山湾区的一名业余摄影师。

74
01:06:51.000 --> 01:08:04.000
Recordings of Wheel's voice were played to those who had heard the real Zodiac speak, including Lake Berryessa survivor Brian Hartnell, and none thought they were the same person. Regardless, Weir was interviewed extensively and also provided fingerprints and handwriting samples. Investigators confirmed he was responsible for the hoax phone calls to the police department, the Jim Dunbar show, and Marvin Belai's residence. But he was ultimately ruled out as a suspect in the Zodiac killings. The real Zodiac never responded to Belai's public offer of assistance. As news of the Zodiac continued to dominate headlines in California, Los Angeles resident Donald Cheney couldn't shake an uneasy feeling. He'd recently been plagued by the memory of something that happened a couple of years earlier, and it was eating at his every thought. In January of 1968, Donald had been on a hunting trip with a friend.
威尔的声音录音被播放给那些听过真正的“黄道十二宫”说话的人听，包括伯耶萨湖幸存者布莱恩·哈特内尔，没有人认为他们是同一个人。无论如何，威尔接受了广泛的采访，并提供了指纹和笔迹样本。调查人员证实，他对警察局、《吉姆·邓巴秀》和马文·贝利住所的恶作剧电话负责。但他最终被排除在“黄道十二宫”谋杀案的嫌疑人之外。真正的“黄道十二宫”从未回应贝利公开提供的帮助。随着“黄道十二宫”的新闻继续占据加州的头条新闻，洛杉矶居民唐纳德·切尼无法摆脱一种不安的感觉。他最近一直被几年前发生的一件事的记忆所困扰，这让他每时每刻都在思考。1968年1月，唐纳德和一位朋友去旅行狩猎。

